IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-increases`

-- TESTS for ssc4-increases.l4 (ss 86A-93; ss 80-86 and s 90 are blank in this text). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- ss 86A to 93`

§§ `s 86A -- incapacity benefit: increase for adult dependants`

-- s 86A(1): in the prescribed circumstances the rates "shall ... be increased ... by the appropriate amount specified" in Schedule 4: the amount (here a test number, 25.5) is the increase.
-- Circumstances not met: the text does not say there is no increase, so NOTHING. Circumstances unknown, or the table figure missing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 25.5) EQUALS JUST 25.5
#ASSERT `s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 25.5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 25.5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 87 -- rate of increase where associated retirement pension is attributable to reduced contributions`

-- s 87(1): (a) entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under s 30A(2)(b) and (b) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of s 60: the amount of the increase is determined under regulations.
-- Either limb missing is not stated to give a different answer: NOTHING. Limb (b) unknown: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 87(2): "The regulations shall not provide for any such increase in a case where" (a) the pension would have been payable only by virtue of s 60 and (b) would have contained no basic pension for failure of a contribution condition.
-- Both: barred (TRUE). Otherwise the sentence says nothing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 87(2) the person is barred from an increase under the regulations` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 87(2) the person is barred from an increase under the regulations` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 87(2) the person is barred from an increase under the regulations` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 87(2) the person is barred from an increase under the regulations` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 88 -- increases to be in respect of only one adult dependant`

-- s 88: not entitled "for the same period to an increase of benefit in respect of more than one person". One person: nothing barred by this sentence (NOTHING). Two or more: barred.
#ASSERT `s 88 the person is barred from an increase in respect of a further person for the same period` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 the person is barred from an increase in respect of a further person for the same period` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 the person is barred from an increase in respect of a further person for the same period` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88 the person is barred from an increase in respect of a further person for the same period` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 89 -- earnings to include occupational and personal pensions etc.`

-- s 89(3): "PPF periodic payments" means (a) periodic compensation payments under the pension compensation provisions; or (b) periodic payments under s 166 of the 2004 Act or Art 150 of the 2005 Order; other than payments made to a surviving dependant.
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 89(1): "Except as may be prescribed", earnings "includes" payments by way of occupational or personal pension. A pension payment with no prescribed exception counts. With a prescribed exception it does not.
-- A payment that is not a pension payment: "includes" is not "means", so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 89(1A): the same for PPF periodic payments.
#ASSERT `s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 91 -- effect of trade disputes on entitlement to increases`

-- s 91(2): "A person falls within this subsection if" (a) prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by s 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995; or (b) would be so prevented if otherwise entitled.
#ASSERT `s 91(2) the person falls within this subsection` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 91(2) the person falls within this subsection` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 91(2) the person falls within this subsection` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 91(2) the person falls within this subsection` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 91(1): "A beneficiary shall not be entitled" to the increase "if the person in respect of whom he would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2)". Falls within: barred (TRUE). Does not: no bar (FALSE). Unknown: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 91(1) the beneficiary is barred from the increase by a trade dispute` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 91(1) the beneficiary is barred from the increase by a trade dispute` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 91(1) the beneficiary is barred from the increase by a trade dispute` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 92 -- dependency increases: continuation of awards in cases of fluctuating earnings`

-- s 92(1): where awarded but ceases to be entitled by reason only of the relevant earner's earnings, "if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled ... disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force".
-- Would have continued: continues. Would not: "if and so long as" gives no continuation (FALSE). Not within the "Where" limbs: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the award continues in force` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the award continues in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the award continues in force` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the award continues in force` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the award continues in force` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 92(1), second limb: "the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, the specified amount".
-- The amount 20: earnings of 20 do not exceed it (no bar); 20.01 exceeds it (barred). If the award does not continue, this sentence is not engaged: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` (JUST TRUE) 20.01 20 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` (JUST TRUE) 20 20 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` (JUST TRUE) 19.99 20 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` (JUST FALSE) 30 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` NOTHING 30 20 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 92(2): the relevant earnings are "those earnings of the relevant earner which, apart from this section, would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase".
#ASSERT `s 92(2) the earnings relevant to the week in pounds` 55.5 TRUE EQUALS JUST 55.5
#ASSERT `s 92(2) the earnings relevant to the week in pounds` 55.5 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 93 -- dependency increases on termination of employment after a period of entitlement to disability working allowance`

-- s 93: the increase "shall be treated as having been payable ... on each day between the last day on which his benefit was previously payable and the day on which he again becomes entitled to it".
-- Last payable 10 January 2025, entitled again 20 January 2025; the two named days are taken to be outside "between" (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 11 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 19 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 9 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 21 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Each of the four named regulations qualifies; some other provision does not.
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(ii) regulation 2 of the Social Security (Savings for Existing Beneficiaries) Regulations 1984` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(iii) regulation 3 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Amendment Regulations 1984` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b)(iv) regulation 4 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency and Computation of Earnings) Amendment Regulations 1989` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 93(b) another provision` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Entitled by virtue of s 42 alone, or of s 30C alone, qualifies; neither (or unknown): the Act does not say, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` NOTHING NOTHING `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
